@echo off
REM ============================================================================
REM MAKE.BAT - assemble lesson 5, from inside DOS.
REM
REM   cd LESSONS\L05
REM   MAKE            ->  TURN.COM  and  PIVOT.COM
REM
REM The lesson itself types the assembler's command line on camera, because
REM watching FASM.EXE be the thing that makes the program is half the point.
REM This file exists for the other times: checking a change without recording
REM anything, and being called by MAKEWIN.BAT from Windows.
REM
REM SINT.INC IS NOT BUILT HERE. It is the output of MKSIN.C, which is a C
REM program compiled by Open Watcom on a machine that has floating point -
REM the generated file is committed precisely so that this build, and the
REM browser bundle, need neither Watcom nor a compiler at all.
REM
REM WHY IT LOADS CWSDPMI. FASM is a 32-bit program, DOS is a 16-bit system,
REM and something has to own protected mode on its behalf; DOSBox offers
REM nothing. CWSDPMI with no arguments stays resident for one program and
REM unloads itself again, so it comes before each assembly.
REM
REM   MAKE EXIT   assembles and then closes DOSBox, for MAKEWIN.BAT.
REM ============================================================================
REM THIS FILE TAKES NO SOURCE NAME, and an attempt to give it one is why
REM there is a RECON.BAT next to it. A batch started from a DOSBox -c line
REM receives %1 and nothing after it, so "MAKE.BAT EXIT RECON" arrives with
REM %2 empty; the file test then fails, the batch exits having assembled
REM NOTHING, and it leaves the previous TURN.COM deleted. Zero bytes, no
REM error, and the next thing that reads it sees an empty program.
if not exist ..\..\TOOLS\FASM\FASM.EXE goto nofasm
if not exist TURN.ASM goto nosource
if not exist SINT.INC goto notable

echo Assembling TURN.ASM ...
if exist TURN.COM del TURN.COM
..\..\TOOLS\CWSDPMI\CWSDPMI.EXE
..\..\TOOLS\FASM\FASM.EXE TURN.ASM TURN.COM
REM "exists" is not "was built": a killed assembler leaves a ZERO-BYTE file
REM behind and this test sails straight past it. There is no tidy way to ask
REM a DOS batch for a file's length - a DIR piped through FIND was tried and
REM it left the emulator sitting at its prompt - so the check lives on the
REM Windows side, in MAKEWIN.BAT, where a shell can do arithmetic.
if not exist TURN.COM goto failed

echo Assembling PIVOT.ASM ...
if exist PIVOT.COM del PIVOT.COM
..\..\TOOLS\CWSDPMI\CWSDPMI.EXE
..\..\TOOLS\FASM\FASM.EXE PIVOT.ASM PIVOT.COM
if not exist PIVOT.COM goto failed

echo.
echo Built TURN.COM.  Type TURN to run it - a key moves to the next frame.
goto end

:nofasm
echo TOOLS\FASM\FASM.EXE not found - run this from LESSONS\L05.
goto end
:nosource
echo TURN.ASM not found - run this from LESSONS\L05.
goto end
:notable
echo SINT.INC not found. It is generated by MKSIN.C and committed; if it
echo really is missing, build MKSIN with Open Watcom and run it.
goto end
:failed
echo.
echo Build failed - see the messages above.
:end
if /i "%~1"=="EXIT" exit
